title: Your own commands
card: Chapter 6 | Your own commands | Giving a job a name
say:
  So far everything has been inside genesis. But you can make new commands of your own.
  Putting a job in its own command gives it a name, so the program reads like a list of what happens.
uncard

new: greet.stella
type:
  genesis:
    greet with "Sam"
    greet with "Ann"
    scrawl "Double 21 is ", double 21
  and the universe said i love you

  to greet, given who (text):
    scrawl "Hello, ", who, "!"
  and the universe said i love you

  to double, given x (a number), returning a number:
    return x times 2
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 7-9
spot: line 7
say:
  To greet makes a command called greet. After the word given come its inputs. This one has one input, called who, and in brackets, the kind of value it is: text.
spot: line 8
say: Inside, who holds whatever it was given.
spot: line 9
say: A command ends with the same line as genesis does.
spot: off
zoom: lines 11-13
spot: line 11
say:
  Double is a command that gives back an answer. Returning a number says what kind of answer.
spot: line 12
say: And return hands the answer back, and leaves the command.
spot: off
zoom: lines 1-4
say:
  Now genesis reads like a story. Greet with Sam. Greet with Ann. Scrawl double twenty one.
  A command can be written before or after the place that uses it.
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 6 | Usual values | Inputs you can leave out
say: An input can have a usual value. Leave it out, and the command gets that value instead.
uncard
select: 7-9
type:
  to greet, given who (text, usually "friend") and count (a number, usually 1):
    repeat count times:
      scrawl "Hello, [who]!"
  and the universe said i love you
keys: enter
zoom: lines 7-10
spot: line 7
say:
  Two inputs now, joined with and. Who is usually friend, and count is usually one.
  Inputs with a usual value go last.
spot: off
line: 3
type:

    greet
    greet with ("Jo", 2)
zoom: lines 2-5
say:
  Greet on its own uses both usual values. With two or more inputs, they go in brackets, in order, with commas.
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
say: Hello Sam, hello Ann, hello friend, and two hellos for Jo.
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 6 | Commands as values | Keeping a command to do later
say:
  A command can even be kept in a name, or given to another command, like any other value.
uncard
clear
type:
  to double, given x (a number), returning a number:
    return x times 2
  and the universe said i love you

  to is big, given x (a number), returning yes or no:
    return x exceeds 10
  and the universe said i love you

  to do twice, given f (a command given a number returning a number) and x (a number), returning a number:
    return invoke f with (invoke f with x)
  and the universe said i love you

  genesis:
    scrawl do twice with (the command double, 5)
    set numbers to a list of (4, 9, 15, 30)
    scrawl numbers changed by the command double
    scrawl numbers kept by the command is big
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 9-11
spot: line 9
say:
  Do twice takes a command as its first input. Its kind says what that command takes and gives back: a command given a number, returning a number.
spot: line 10
say: Invoke does the command it was given. Here it does it twice: once on x, and then again on the answer.
spot: off
zoom: lines 13-18
spot: line 14
say:
  The command double, with the word the in front, is the command itself, not its answer. So do twice, with double and five, is double of double of five: twenty.
spot: lines 16-17
say:
  Changed by does a command to every item of a list, and kept by keeps only the items a command says yes to.
spot: off
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
say: Twenty. Every number doubled. And just the big ones.
wait
zoom: out

say:
  One more way to write inputs: when a command has many, they can go on their own lines, under the word use, before its instructions.
clear
type:
  to tell, use:
    title (text)
    count (a number)

    scrawl title, " times ", count
  and the universe said i love you

  genesis:
    tell with "apples", 3
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 1-6
say: Each input on its own line, a blank line, and then what the command does.
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
wait
zoom: out
